WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.400
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.520
Did you know that eight threads of
saffron a day can improve visual acuity

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.000
in older adults with mild or moderate
age-related macular degeneration?

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.840
Here’s the first story.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.000
In addition to two
to three daily servings

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.680
of green leafy vegetables,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.920
berries are considered
a healthy choice

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.960
for the preservation
of eye health.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.800
As we age, our critical
retinal pigment epithelium layer

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.160
starts to break down.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.040
However, we may be able
to decelerate that aging

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.480
with blueberries.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.760
Human RPE cells bathed in
blueberry anthocyanins

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.960
had fewer free radicals

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.880
and a lower proportion
of aged cells,

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.920
suggesting that blueberries
and other red, blue, and purple

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.440
pigmented fruits and vegetables

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.360
may help prevent age-related
macular degeneration.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.840
Protective properties
have also been demonstrated

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.360
in vitro on RPE cells

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.000
from purple
sweet potato anthocyanin

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.800
as well as the yellow pigment
in turmeric and an amla extract

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.480
(Indian gooseberry).

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.960
However, the only
human interventional trials

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.000
on berries for vision
were a month-long trial

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.320
of a bilberry extract
that demonstrated

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.080
significantly less eye strain

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.720
after iPad use
compared to placebo

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.200
and a study showing
three weeks of blueberry juice

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.040
or freeze-dried blueberry powder

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.800
both significantly improved
photostress recovery time,

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.840
which is the time needed
to recuperate visual acuity

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.520
after bright light exposure

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.440
by about five seconds.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.840
Only one pigmented food
has been put to the test

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.400
in macular
degeneration patients:

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.880
the spice saffron.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.360
Saffron is so potent
that the whole spice

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.760
can be stuffed into capsules
to pit them head-to-head

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.360
against placebo.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.560
Those with early-stage
age-related macular degeneration

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.840
were randomized to a tiny pinch
(20 mg, about 8 threads)

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:07.280
of saffron versus placebo
for three months.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.880
Compared to the placebo group,

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.200
the saffron group experienced
a significant improvement

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.600
in retinal flicker sensitivity--

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.880
that’s our ability to pick out

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.560
high frequency light pulses

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.160
(rather than seeing
the flickering light

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.520
as a steady beam)

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.440
that diminishes with age.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.000
It’s a sensitive test
of retinal function,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.400
but it is of questionable
clinical value.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.160
However, there was
a small improvement

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.520
in visual acuity in 80 percent
of the saffron subjects

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.640
(being able to see one line
further down on an eye chart)

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.040
versus none improving
in the placebo group.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:37.920
This is particularly important

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.200
for those with age-related

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.400
macular degeneration

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.440
for whom vision tends
to get worse over time,

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.200
not better.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.200
What about a more
substantial pinch?

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.040
(50 mg, about 20 threads)

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.160
Compared to placebo,
three months of this larger dose

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.560
led to a similar
improvement in visual acuity

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.360
in macular degeneration
patients, suggesting more

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.360
is not necessarily better.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.920
Saffron is the most
expensive spice there is,

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.000
selling for about $200
an ounce (28 g),

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.640
so being able to get away
with a 20 mg dose

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.400
(about 15 cents a day)

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.560
rather than a 50 mg dose
(closer to 40 cents a day)

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.040
could add up over the long run.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.040
Even smaller doses may work too,

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.360
but they just
haven’t been tested.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.440
What about
the tiny pinch over a year

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.120
instead of just three months?

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.160
Early-stage macular patients
were given 20 mg of saffron

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.400
a day for an average
of 14 months

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.840
and average visual acuity

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.640
improved by two eye chart lines.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.640
They also reported
an improvement in contrast

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.960
and color perception,
reading ability,

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:37.840
low-light vision,

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.160
and overall quality of life.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.560
The problem is the study
lacked a control group,

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.240
so it’s hard to put much stock

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:47.120
in subjective measures
of improvement.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.760
Interestingly, a six-month
randomized, double-blind,

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.040
placebo-controlled trial

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.680
found no objective
acuity improvement

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:55.280
in either the placebo group

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:58.080
or a 30 mg a day saffron group,

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.400
yet reported that the patients

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.480
unwittingly in the saffron group

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.960
gave subjective reports
of better vision

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.040
and general wellbeing.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.320
The researchers suggest

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.480
this may be an
antidepressant effect,

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.960
and indeed a meta-analysis
of a dozen

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.440
randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trials

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.320
of saffron for depression
found it beat out placebo

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.600
and was found comparable
to antidepressant drugs.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.240
The largest saffron
vision trial to date

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.160
was a double-blind,
placebo-controlled

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.480
crossover trial
in which 100 older adults

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.480
with mild or moderate

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.400
age-related macular degeneration

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.720
were randomized to 20 mg
of saffron a day

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.320
or placebo for three months,

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.920
then switched
to the opposite group

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.840
for an additional three months.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.560
When on the tiny
daily pinch of saffron

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.200
there was a significant,
yet modest improvement

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.480
in visual acuity,

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:49.440
and this was the case
for both those on and off

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.200
best practice therapy

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.240
(the beta-carotene free
AREDS supplementation),

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.760
suggesting an additive benefit.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:58.640
In our next story,

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:02.560
we look at the effects of both
oral and topical application

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:06.880
of the spice saffron
for male impotence.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.160
The spice saffron has traditionally
been considered an aphrodisiac.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:19.440
It has been shown to improve Prozac-induced
sexual dysfunction in women and men,

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.320
significantly improving
erectile function.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:26.080
If it works for drug-induced
dysfunction,

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:30.160
might it work for just
regular erectile dysfunction?

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.040
Why not just use
pills like Viagra?

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:37.040
They can work, but many men stop
using them due to, for example,

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.800
adverse side-effects.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.320
Nearly half of men decide
the cons outweigh the pros.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.320
For men that don’t like
drugs there’s always surgery,

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.240
the implantation of
penile prosthetics.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:59.120
Unbelievably, penile implant usage
evidently dates back to the 16th century.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.880
Early experiments involved
transplanting a guy’s rib cartilage,

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.880
or their actual rib
into their penis.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:10.000
Thankfully space-age
technologies in the 60s

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.920
allowed men to keep
their ribcages intact.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:18.880
Originally the implants left men
in a permanently erect state,

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:23.440
but then the Flexirod was invented
with a hinge in the middle

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:28.880
so the guy could like bend it
down in half for improved concealment.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.120
Of course, proper
sizing is important.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.560
If the implants are too small there
can be drooping at the tip

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:38.960
leading to what’s called a
“supersonic transport deformity.”

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.160
Why?

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:45.600
“Because of its resemblance
to the nose of the Concorde” jet.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:48.800
Whereas “overlong prostheses
can also be a problem,

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.680
with the semi-rigid rods
[eroding]” out of the penis.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.640
Although they generally
perforate into the urethra,

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.400
the rods can also extrude through
the tip or the shaft.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:02.560
Ouch.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.800
Now there are inflatable
devices, and perhaps one day

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:11.360
there will be “expandable foams that
respond to external magnetic fields”

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:17.280
or metal mesh technology that could expand
and retract in a cage-like fashion.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:21.040
And you thought it was hard to
get through airport security now.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.800
There’s got to
be a better way.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:27.360
Twenty men with erectile dysfunction
were followed for ten days

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:31.360
taking 200 mg of saffron a day—
that’s about a quarter teaspoon—

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:34.800
but first they were brought
into the RigiScan room,

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:38.400
where they were hooked up to a computer
controlled, battery-powered system

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:43.520
for recording of penile tumescence,
meaning swelling and rigidity.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:47.200
You can hook men up and have
them watch a VHS video tape,

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.560
though use of the device is
controversial, described as an

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.920
“expensive, complicated, and
time-consuming effort.”

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:58.880
But after the ten days of taking saffron there
did appear to be a significant improvement

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:02.240
in tip and base rigidity
and tumescence.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:06.320
Whether it’s possible to replace
Viagra-type drugs with this golden plant

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:09.680
will require "further research
with a bigger sample size.”

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:13.040
But it’s not just size that matters,
they didn’t use a control,

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.120
so this could have all just
been one big placebo effect.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:22.640
Finally, though, a head-to-head
challenge—saffron versus Viagra.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.920
Now normally there’s a third
group—a placebo group, as well—

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.000
but evidently, they felt
it would be unethical

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:32.880
to let men go 12 weeks
without an effective treatment.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.640
The saffron appeared safer,
significantly fewer side-effects

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:41.280
like severe headaches, hot flushes,
nasal congestion and nausea…

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:44.160
but not effective at all.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:50.080
So that’s why I never did a video on
the subject—it just doesn’t seem to help.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:54.320
But maybe it’s because they made the
mistake of taking the saffron orally,

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:58.160
as opposed to rubbing
it on their penis.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:02.480
The effects of topical saffron
on erectile dysfunction.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:05.840
About half of middle-aged
men appear to suffer.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:09.680
So how about a randomized double-
blind placebo-controlled study.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:12.880
A gel containing 1% saffron,
or instead of saffron,

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:18.400
a gel containing a little golden yellow
food coloring so they looked the same.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.920
Though presumably, half the
penises smelled like paella;

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:24.560
I guess they didn’t
control for that.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:29.200
“Both groups were trained to rub a pea-sized
amount of the gel on their penis

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:34.080
half an hour before sexual intercourse”
and then were re-assessed a month later.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:38.720
And, compared to the food coloring gel,
the saffron did lead to significant

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:42.560
improvements in function, and
desire, and overall satisfaction.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:45.200
They attribute the effects
to a compound in saffron

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:50.000
that evidently enhances nitric oxide
production in the arteries.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.960
But if that’s the case, then
probably better to treat the cause

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:00.560
and prevent the vascular
dysfunction in the first place.

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:01.440
Finally today,

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:06.080
the spice saffron appears to improve both
the emotional and physical symptoms

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.560
of PMS, premenstrual syndrome.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.800
Here’s the story.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.360
PMS is “among the most common
health problems reported by women,”

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:17.440
affecting approximately one&nbsp;in three,

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:21.360
and there’s not much
modern medicine has to offer.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:24.080
Ancient traditional medicine,
though, in Asia and Persia,

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:27.760
used a spice called saffron
to treat menstrual disorders.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:28.920
But, what did they know?

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:31.200
And, that was 3,500 years ago—

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.960
in fact, the earliest recorded
use of any medicinal plant.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:37.040
Didn’t they know, though,
that you can’t really know anything

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:40.880
unless it’s put through a double-blind,
randomized, placebo-controlled trial?

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:45.840
Well, it took 3,500 years,
but we finally have it.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:48.160
Women experiencing PMS
for at least six&nbsp;months

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.640
were randomly assigned
to a capsule of saffron,

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:54.000
versus a capsule of nothing,
and lo and behold,

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:59.360
“saffron was found to be effective in relieving
symptoms of PMS.”

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.000
Check it out.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.560
Reported PMS symptoms
significantly dropped

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.080
even within the first cycle,
and continued to improve.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:10.000
This included changes in “mood
(anxiety, irritability,

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.320
depression, nervous tension,
mood swings and

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:16.640
[feelings of being] out of control),
behaviour (poor coordination,

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.960
insomnia, confusion,
headache, crying and fatigue),

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.200
pain (aches, cramps and tenderness)

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:24.800
and [other] physical [symptoms
including]… craving[s] and swelling)…”

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:30.000
All thanks to a little spice,
from the saffron crocus.

